# The website's settings. Copy to .env.local for development; in production
# set them on the host (e.g. AWS) as environment variables.

# The backend's address. Used when the site is built (it pre-renders pages and
# sets up forwarding of /api/admin, /api/v1 and /uploads from it) and while it
# runs, so the backend must be running and reachable at build time too.
# Already set per mode in .env.development (http://127.0.0.1:4000) and
# host only to override them. Always https:// for a remote backend.
# BACKEND_URL=

# Same value as SPARK_SHARED_SECRET in the backend's settings. Lets the backend
# tell the site to refresh after a publish, and lets the site read drafts for
# preview mode. A long random string:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
SPARK_SHARED_SECRET=

# Optional. Leave empty (recommended): the admin calls /api/admin on this site,
# which forwards it to BACKEND_URL, so there's no CORS. Set it to the backend's
# public HTTPS address to have the admin call the backend directly instead; then
# add this site's address to FRONTEND_URL or CORS_ORIGINS in the backend's settings.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=
